{
  "_comment": [
    "Twinned tally fixture (WS9-052). Read by BOTH core/review's TestTallyTwinFixture and the web",
    "tier's review.test.ts, so the Go and TypeScript tallies are checked against ONE set of numbers",
    "rather than two independently-authored ones.",
    "",
    "The tally is derived rather than transmitted: a run's document carries per-item outcomes, and each",
    "surface counts them itself. That is cheap and avoids a redundant wire field, but it means the two",
    "implementations can disagree, and a disagreement here is not cosmetic. `covered` is the number a",
    "team reads as 'how much of our checklist is actually mechanised', so a client that counted",
    "not-automated as covered would report a checklist as answered when nobody had answered it.",
    "",
    "Adding an outcome to the vocabulary means adding a case here first. If only one side is updated",
    "the fixture fails on the other, which is the point."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "empty",
      "outcomes": [],
      "want": {
        "pass": 0, "fail": 0, "notApplicable": 0, "notAutomated": 0,
        "provisional": 0, "needsDesignIntent": 0, "computedNA": 0,
        "needsData": 0, "inconclusive": 0,
        "total": 0, "covered": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "plain pass fail",
      "outcomes": ["pass", "pass", "fail"],
      "want": {
        "pass": 2, "fail": 1, "notApplicable": 0, "notAutomated": 0,
        "provisional": 0, "needsDesignIntent": 0, "computedNA": 0,
        "needsData": 0, "inconclusive": 0,
        "total": 3, "covered": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "not-automated is the only outcome that is not covered",
      "outcomes": ["pass", "not-automated", "not-automated", "not-applicable"],
      "want": {
        "pass": 1, "fail": 0, "notApplicable": 1, "notAutomated": 2,
        "provisional": 0, "needsDesignIntent": 0, "computedNA": 0,
        "needsData": 0, "inconclusive": 0,
        "total": 4, "covered": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "every verdict in the vocabulary once",
      "outcomes": [
        "pass", "fail", "not-applicable", "not-automated",
        "provisional", "needs-design-intent", "computed-n/a",
        "needs-data", "inconclusive"
